{"uuid":"54D3937B-C92F-5483-A127-43B2986429AF","name":"Teriyaki Chicken","serves":10,"duration":15,"cookingDuration":210,"defaultScale":1,"isPublicRecipe":false,"folderIDs":[],"ingredients":[{"uuid":"704CB778-20C7-5AA2-9E50-D10440C13CCF","order":0,"ingredient":{"uuid":"6267B6EE-3B95-5677-A006-DCF72AC0BF9D","name":"chicken breast, whole (not cubed)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"POUND","amount":4.5}},{"uuid":"825CBF58-9042-568A-832E-FB5932F840B6","order":1,"ingredient":{"uuid":"97510C68-24DF-5489-99C1-7DFE5705687B","name":"chicken broth"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":0.5}},{"uuid":"D0734C61-9BC4-5F9A-8F5C-2E8E34A22DDE","order":2,"ingredient":{"uuid":"AA47E063-22A0-596A-90E0-655F127B5656","name":"jasmine rice (dry)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":3.5}},{"uuid":"0319567F-2BA1-5421-9E25-CFFEC7A997B5","order":3,"ingredient":{"uuid":"92CB2AF5-8E39-5C75-A657-7EAA180E80AF","name":"broccoli florets (yields ~1200 g roasted)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"POUND","amount":5.5}},{"uuid":"56FC8DE4-D0D9-5E5A-8260-6CA366C08E0D","order":4,"ingredient":{"uuid":"EE00356D-8621-51AF-B0C3-D134C075B961","name":"bottles teriyaki sauce (~422 g total)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":2}},{"uuid":"1CE034F3-EE4D-510B-BF94-6C0EA7169D08","order":5,"ingredient":{"uuid":"07501558-0B84-5BE2-9346-28BF7F332C17","name":"Olive oil, salt, pepper"}}],"steps":[{"uuid":"E9531496-0846-5FB4-9EC7-6A9132829EDE","order":0,"step":"Place 4 ½ lbs whole chicken breasts in the crockpot. Season with salt and pepper and add ½ cup chicken broth for moisture. No cutting required.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"3E8D70B2-1313-5FFD-945F-B0B6625A8EA3","order":1,"step":"Cook on High 3–4 hours, or Low 6–7 hours, until the chicken reaches 165°F and is fork-tender.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"5B960096-2965-5D43-B0A9-EC2D2C30B0C9","order":2,"step":"Drain the cooking liquid. Draining prevents a watery result once the sauce goes on.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"8088DCE2-4CF5-5B0E-BBE5-A874DF67AAD8","order":3,"step":"Shred the chicken with a hand mixer directly in the crockpot — this takes about 30 seconds. A few pulses is enough; over-mixing turns it mushy.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"7F652A94-0D4B-5683-808E-70989AF42369","order":4,"step":"During the last ~20 minutes of chicken time, rinse 3 ½ cups jasmine rice 2–3 times until the water runs mostly clear. Add to the Instant Pot with 3 ½ cups water (1:1).","isSection":false},{"uuid":"DC360E47-FB8E-52FC-83EA-D19A267721EC","order":5,"step":"Confirm the valve is set to SEALING. Pressure Cook (Manual) on High for 3 minutes, natural release 10 minutes, then quick release. Fluff and leave the lid off to cool.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"75C246E1-0F6A-54CB-97E3-8F6628A765D3","order":6,"step":"Toss the broccoli with olive oil, salt, and pepper. Air roast at 400°F in the Ninja toaster oven for 12–15 minutes until the edges are slightly crispy. Do this in 2 batches — 5 ½ lbs will not fit in a single layer.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"E012E914-2BE3-5982-B618-7070242D3700","order":7,"step":"Let the chicken, rice, and broccoli cool 10–15 minutes before portioning. Spread the rice on a sheet pan to cool it faster.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"0950BDE0-8DAE-51EA-B30E-5AF2CED87B74","order":8,"step":"Assembly line across 10 open containers: 145 g chicken, then 140 g rice, then 120 g broccoli.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"8AF3B75F-3432-5F81-BC15-93565431F892","order":9,"step":"Portion ~42 g teriyaki sauce into 10 separate small containers. The sauce is packed separately here — adding it before storage makes the rice soggy by day 2.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"21A7845F-1B3D-5FBC-84D5-4D51919E8511","order":10,"step":"Label with a dry-erase marker. 6 containers to the fridge, 4 to the freezer. Move freezer containers to the fridge the night before eating.","isSection":false}],"notes":"UNTESTED — v2, never cooked\n\nPER CONTAINER (10 total)\n  chicken: 145 g\n  rice: 140 g\n  broccoli: 120 g\n  sauce: 42 g\n  total: 447 g\n\nSTORAGE: 6 fridge, 4 freezer\nFreezer containers move to the fridge the night before eating.\n\nUNTESTED IN THIS FORM — v2 switched from cubed oven-roasted chicken to whole\nbreasts in the crockpot, so quantities are planned, not observed. Weigh the\nshredded chicken, the cooked rice, and the roasted broccoli, then promote with\na real date.\n\nWhy crockpot: cubed chicken measured 0.409 last session, the bottom of its\nrange. Hitting 145 g per container that way needs 7.8 lbs of chicken; whole\nbreasts at 0.72 need about 4 ½. Trade-off is shredded rather than cubed and no\nseared edges — the sauce carries it.\n\nBroccoli takes 5 ½ lbs, not the 3 ½–4 an earlier version called for; measured\nyield is 0.48. It will not fit the toaster oven in one layer, so plan on\n2 batches.\n\nSauce: 422 g across 10 containers is 42 g each. An earlier note said \"~50 g\neach\", which does not divide. If 50 g is what it actually takes to coat a\nbowl, that is a third bottle and ~500 mg more sodium. Settle it this cook.\n\nSodium is the problem here — ~1400 mg per container, nearly double the\nceiling, essentially all from the bottled sauce. Honey garlic is the worked\nexample of the fix: scratch sauce lands at 700 mg.\n\nSauce is packed separately so the rice does not go soggy. Add it after\nreheating — air fryer 350°F, 5–7 minutes. Rice and chicken freeze well;\nbroccoli softens slightly but holds.","neutritionalInfo":"Serving Size: 1 container,\nCalories: 540 kcal,\nProtein: 52 g,\nCarbohydrates: 60 g,\nFat: 11 g,\nFiber: 4 g,\nSodium: 1400 mg,\nSugar: 12 g","sourceName":"ten-containers","webLink":"https://zjbecker32.github.io/ten-containers/recipes/teriyaki-chicken/","tags":[],"images":[]}